ss 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution, only partial.\n\nEvidence: Dashboarding adds value after logs exist but does not itself guarantee the mandatory automatic recording capability required by Article 12(1).\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree to which idea is not only rare but ingenious...\nProposal is log analytics dashboard for clients. That's common in industry. Probably common, mundane. Originality 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nEvidence: Hosted log analytics dashboards for compliance monitoring are a common SaaS offering and standard practice in regulated industries.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm.\nParadigm breaking = introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. Paradigm stretching = changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance). Slightly paradigm stretching = introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Paradigm preserving = standard compliance.\n\nProposal converts mandatory obligation into visible monitoring service differentiating lab in procurement and demonstrates diligence. That is new partners/offerings born from compliance. Changes relationship. That's paradigm stretching: changes that relationship e.g., new partners or offerings born from compliance. So level 3.\n\nEvidence: Turning required logging into a client-facing monitoring service creates a new commercial offering derived from compliance.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nSome changes, reasonably feasible measures? Data engineers build streaming pipeline... Compliance analysts configure threshold alerts. That's significant change, expensive or difficult but not totally impossible. Could be 2 or 3. \"some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\" = 3. Might be significant change? Building hosted platform is significant. Maybe 2 = significant change, or expensive or difficult, but not totally impossible. Hmm.\n\nThe lab must commit scarce implementation resources. Building streaming pipeline and hosted platform is non-trivial. I'd say significant change, expensive. So implementability 2.\n\nEvidence: Deploying a hosted streaming ingestion pipeline with configurable risk alerts requires dedicated data engineering and compliance staffing beyond routine logging.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms = 4. It's monitoring service. Possibly raises data privacy concerns? Logging high-risk AI may involve personal data. Providing dashboard to clients may be acceptable. Probably common strategies that violate no norms. So acceptability 4.\n\nEvidence: Offering post-market monitoring dashboards aligns with regulatory expectations and does not violate legal or business norms.\n\nReturn rating echo id exactly.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably JSON? Not specified but likely output lines. Provide in order.\n\nProbably produce:\n\nid P2155\napplicability_evidence ...\napplicability 4\netc.\n\nLet's output clearly.\n\n",
