ures. Solves identified problem directly related? It aims to meet logging mandate via research, producing design patterns. That's directly related. Might be 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Doing research to find best logging architecture applies.\n\nEvidence: the track directly targets Article 12 logging requirements by investigating event-capture granularity and retention for high-risk systems.\n\nScore 4? Could be 3 solves implied problem. Hmm. It does apply. I'd give 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nWill research programme ensure compliance now? It studies optimal architectures over 18 months, not immediate implementation. It will contribute to solution but is partial and delayed. Reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem, it helps but only partial. Score 3.\n\nEvidence: an 18-month research track can yield better logging designs but does not itself deploy compliant logging for current systems.\n\nScore 3.\n\nacceptability (1-4): degree socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies violate no norms. Research, publishing open benchmarks, seeking EU funding is acceptable. Score 4.\n\nEvidence: internal research, open benchmarks and Horizon co-funding pursuit conform to normal academic and regulatory norms.\n\nScore 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\nDedicate one postdoc and modest GPU for 18 months, targeting co-funding offsets cost. Some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Not easy low cost? Modest cost but still requires personnel. Probably 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures.\n\nEvidence: staffing one postdoc and modest compute is a limited, feasible reallocation within tight fiscal ceilings with planned co-funding.\n\nScore 3.\n\nReturn JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably o