: 4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. 3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...). 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance.\n\nThis proposal weaves lineage into reproducibility methodology and publication pipeline, strengthening both compliance posture and publication. That changes relationship between R&D and compliance obligations – logging woven into science. Might be paradigm stretching: changes that relationship. Could be 3. Or slightly paradigm stretching 2? It introduces new elements (tools) but still treats compliance as logging practice? It says contributes original methodology to reproducibility literature, strengthening publication pipeline. That's more than just logging practice. I think paradigm stretching = 3.\n\nLet's assign:\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building a cryptographic hash-chain ledger and audit protocols requires new infrastructure integration but is feasible with existing engineering resources. => score 3\n\nacceptability_evidence: Verifiable data lineage and public benchmarking for compliance align with regulatory expectations and scientific norms without violating legal or ethical sensibilities. => 4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The lineage system audits reference-database drift and supports traceability for Article 12(3)(b) but does not by itself provide automatic per-use event logs required by Article 12(1)-(2). => 3? Actually effectiveness rating 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution. Evidence says partial.\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly targets the Annex III 1(a) logging minimums for biometric identification systems mandated by Article 12. => 4\n\noriginality_evidence: Combining cryptographic hash-chain ledgers with drift detection benchmarks for biometric reference databases is unusual and shows imagination beyond routine logging. => 3\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It weaves compliance logging into a reproducibility research program and publication pipeline, changing how R&D and compliance obligations relate. => 3\n\nReturn JSON? Format requested: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\". Probably output list.\n\nProvide id echo.\n\nLet's produce.\n\n",
